      "writtenOn": "2023-11-14T04:23:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the user could have the inconsistent state if the user stop or start receiving the callback at some point.   \nThough this depends on how the user maintain the internal state reported by this callback.\n\nIn general, it\u0027s recommended to read flag value only once at initialization, since we faced the issue by the code that reads the flag value multiple times.\nSo, I prefer to call the `isTetheringFeatureNotChickenedOut` in the constructor and store the value.\n\nAs a reference, some codes which read the flag values and store to the fields.\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/h/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Connectivity/service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java;l\u003d1834-1837",
      "parentUuid": "f7bfd42c_45afd9b5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11370,
        "startChar": 30,
